e could recover all territory occupied by Russia. \"With geopolitical turbulence and economic uncertainty driving safe-haven demand, alongside growing expectations of a dovish Fed, gold (should) consolidate above $3,750 in the short term, with the prospect of a new resistance around $3,900,\" said Ricardo Evangelista, senior analyst at ActivTrades.",
